        "coverage": "The original bibliography contains 53 works from 1967\u20132024, only four from 2020 onward and none after 2024. The prior 26 available PDFs cover 1996\u20132024, with most dated 1996\u20132021; three are from 2020 onward. The October 28, 2026 sweep searched 2018\u20132026 literature on contextualism, relativism, expressivism, dynamic semantics, epistemic contradictions, probability operators, retraction and assessment sensitivity. It selected 25 recent works and obtained 17 exact full texts, plus three previously missing originals; 46 PDFs are now local in total. Coverage includes recent surveys, formal models, empirical tests and responses, but eight selected recent works and 24 originals remain unavailable to this client. Older foundational chapters, complete books, the strongest 2024 safety/expressivism comparisons and recent empirical reviews remain material access gaps. This is a ranked, bounded search of indexes and public sources, not an exhaustive review. A failed search or inaccessible paper does not establish an open problem or novelty. The old lack-of-model/test claim is addressed; the other two flagged problems are partially addressed. Acquired files have not been extracted into the frozen ARA evidence: existing route verdicts and generated arguments therefore retain their original evidential limits.",
